  "worked_solution": "A rotation of ${45}^{\u2218}$ *counterclockwise* about the origin is represented by the matrix \n\n$$\n{R}_{({45}^{\u2218})}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({45}^{\u2218}) & -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({45}^{\u2218}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061({45}^{\u2218}) & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061({45}^{\u2218})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image ${v}^{\u2032}$ under the action of the matrix ${R}_{({45}^{\u2218})}$, we compute the matrix product, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{\u2032} & ={R}_{({45}^{\u2218})}\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image is ${v}^{\u2032}=\u27e84\\sqrt{2},-\\sqrt{2}\u27e9.$",
